; TWOMOD.LNK - the link, in a file instead of on the command line.
;
; TANREN reads this when it is given @TWOMOD, and the words in it are
; the words it would have read from the command line. A ; starts a
; comment and the rest of the line is ignored.
;
; MSX-DOS gives a command line 127 characters and cuts a longer one
; without saying so. That is the whole reason this exists: the
; assembler is itself linked from a file of nineteen module names.

/o:twomod.com

main.tro putstr.tro
